                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wax",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87d3995c-4470-314c-a12c-c2921c3f8aa2",
                                        "entry_id": "edd5a874-16d3-3f47-9a39-9f19acccd3f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To apply wax to (something, such as a shoe, a floor, a car, or an apple), usually to make it shiny."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea11ab98-249f-3a04-bb56-e20652a5aed3",
                                        "entry_id": "edd5a874-16d3-3f47-9a39-9f19acccd3f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To remove hair at the roots from (a part of the body) by coating the skin with a film of wax that is then pulled away sharply."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce17d91e-81c5-3830-949a-e6030f99a875",
                                        "entry_id": "edd5a874-16d3-3f47-9a39-9f19acccd3f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To defeat utterly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9a16a49-fb25-334c-9527-a16b2ad78897",
                                        "entry_id": "edd5a874-16d3-3f47-9a39-9f19acccd3f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To kill, especially to murder a person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f64731d7-56eb-43fa-bebf-324e0d6f67c7",
                                                "sense_id": "c9a16a49-fb25-334c-9527-a16b2ad78897",
                                                "text": "\"I was reassigned over from the 9th when the battalion CO got waxed on the road leading in.\" Ben kept his dismay to himself. Here was one more officer in the 90th who'd been on the job only hours or days, replacing commanders killed or wounded...."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18a6e95b-7fb9-4b28-8207-82229df91656",
                                                "sense_id": "c9a16a49-fb25-334c-9527-a16b2ad78897",
                                                "text": "\"You telling me you know who really waxed him and your mom?\"\n \"Yeah,\" she lied.\n \"Just who pulled the trigger or who ordered it to be pulled?\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66411245-7ba2-3cb7-b130-a8609b7e8d70",
                                        "entry_id": "edd5a874-16d3-3f47-9a39-9f19acccd3f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To record."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wax",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6cad36f4-0fd3-3f22-9ec1-60e90544c541",
                                        "entry_id": "39733be9-41a2-3dcb-a106-5e24e6b234d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To greaten."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3bd5052-8a78-4b76-bc0d-aa8867577cc9",
                                                "sense_id": "6cad36f4-0fd3-3f22-9ec1-60e90544c541",
                                                "text": "Holonym: wax and wane"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "399f830f-629e-4270-9829-edaacae8a76c",
                                                "sense_id": "6cad36f4-0fd3-3f22-9ec1-60e90544c541",
                                                "text": "And then the whole quire hold their hips and laugh,\n And waxen in their mirth and neeze and swear\n A merrier hour was never wasted there."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf1637b2-5f3e-42cd-b9c5-2e4805c80154",
                                                "sense_id": "6cad36f4-0fd3-3f22-9ec1-60e90544c541",
                                                "text": "For nature, crescent, does not grow alone\n In thews and bulks, but, as this temple waxes, The inward service of the mind and soul\n Grows wide withal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55e1817e-d563-40a8-8d19-e051a6a2f0ab",
                                                "sense_id": "6cad36f4-0fd3-3f22-9ec1-60e90544c541",
                                                "text": "And so it had always pleased M. Stutz to expect great things from the dark young man whom he had first seen in his early twenties ; and his expectations had waxed rather than waned on hearing the faint bruit of the love of Ivor and Virginia—for Virginia, M. Stutz thought, would bring fineness to a point in a man like Ivor Marlay, […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                        "entry_id": "39733be9-41a2-3dcb-a106-5e24e6b234d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To increasingly assume the specified characteristic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "copulative",
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f40c9e3-4ff1-4826-b7e5-a88c8b3aca23",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "to wax poetic",
                                                "translation": "to become increasingly verbose",
                                                "english": "to become increasingly verbose"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99c107da-80ba-414c-ba94-64a2f85a9d7a",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "to wax wode",
                                                "translation": "to become angry",
                                                "english": "to become angry"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8d7c3b3-7919-41a8-af38-a5c913106453",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "to wax eloquent"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79dc5e9c-f4bd-4315-8388-6e5845ad232f",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "Ah, ſirrah, by my ſay, it waxes late:\n I’ll to my reſt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed88c943-4a42-412f-bb68-00fd96d4f499",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "He waxes desperate with imagination."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96f48d83-09ec-4690-a5c2-a9ad3506575c",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "As a cage is full of birds, so are their houses full of deceit: therefore they are become great, and waxen rich."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b53b0c3-b717-4e84-9dcf-5b5504260209",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "You behold, Sir, how he waxeth Wroth at your Abode here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa8dc45e-0df4-4a51-b53e-81ae1cba09ac",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "The stars grew pale and paler still till at last they vanished; the golden moon waxed wan, and her mountain ridges stood out against her sickly face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68abda80-941d-43f1-9faf-e17decca8c35",
                                                "sense_id": "3cafaac1-2728-3b69-bd81-e9674589cb79",
                                                "text": "In the night, or the gloomy chambers of the day, fears and misgivings wax strong, but out in the sunlight there is, for a time, cessation even of the terror of death."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "338498f2-f709-3397-a92d-4abc75e94b7d",
                                        "entry_id": "39733be9-41a2-3dcb-a106-5e24e6b234d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To appear larger each night as a progression from a new moon to a full moon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c69bee59-738e-358a-8627-cb4eb629cd10",
                                        "entry_id": "39733be9-41a2-3dcb-a106-5e24e6b234d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move from low tide to high tide."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
